We examine the production of heavy neutral leptons (HNLs) within the decay of $B$ mesons, specifically focusing on the channels $B 	o K^{(*)} 
u_i  ar{
u}_j$ and $B 	o \pi 
u_i  ar{
u}_j$. We demonstrate that the mixing angle $|U_e|^2$ can be extracted from these processes by analyzing the charge of the accompanying lepton in the HNL decay. This approach is viable even when the HNL mass is below the kinematic threshold for $e^+e^-$ pair production.
